e.

=E2=80=9CMore and more players are now staying through until they=E2=80=99r=
e having families =E2=80=A6 And they put all this money into research,=E2=
=80=9D she says. They have identified =E2=80=9Cclear cut=E2=80=9D physical =
and mental health benefits for women to keep up with football, including a =
lower injury risk postpartum.

=E2=80=9CThere=E2=80=99s always been a notion that women just aren=E2=80=99=
t strong and robust the way we actually are, and now the science is proving=
 otherwise,=E2=80=9D Dufour says. =E2=80=9CI do think some of it relates to=
 the foetus. That=E2=80=99s going to supersede what=E2=80=99s actually good=
 for the woman, right?=E2=80=9D

Some of the main considerations players should have, whether professional o=
r amateur, as to whether they should keep playing and training throughout p=
regnancy, relate to pain, pelvic floor dysfunction, and motor control and m=
ovement, she adds. But the decision whether or not to continue playing duri=
ng pregnancy is ultimately personal.

When
