ass, but he=E2=80=99s unattached now and is the only unemployed manager who=
 would universally be seen as an upgrade over Pochettino.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Then again, the reasons that made Pochetti=
no lasting a full four years in this job seem outlandish are even more rele=
vant to Guardiola, who turned down the Italy job this summer. While Concaca=
f has improved over the past decade, it=E2=80=99s still among the world=E2=
=80=99s least esteemed confederations and lacks the hallowed continental ch=
ampionships of Europe, South America, Africa and Asia. Would three and a ha=
lf years of friendlies, an easier World Cup qualifying path than ever, and =
routine matchups with Mexico and Canada be enough to whet his competitive a=
ppetite until 2030?</p>
