<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In between Berhalter=E2=80=99s first and s=
econd terms, <strong>BJ Callaghan</strong> led the US to win the Gold Cup w=
ith eye-catching play and impressive control over games. He took his first =
club head coaching job in 2024, and has since turned Nashville SC into a re=
cord-setting team favored to win a rare domestic double this postseason.</p=
>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Nashville signed Callaghan to a fresh exte=
nsion in February, locking him into terms through the 2028-29 MLS season. H=
is possession-heavy style of play remains en vogue in the international gam=
e. But at this stage, the 45-year-old may revel in his current project for =
a bit longer.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>Steve Cherundolo</strong>, a forme=
r US defender and the current U-20/U-23 boss, won an MLS Cup, but his Los A=
ngeles FC tenure was more largely characterized by tactical timidness and f=
ailing to dictate proceedings in the biggest games.</p>
